WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.300
Speaker 1: Yet another Republican has been caught&nbsp;
committing voter fraud. A Republican's wife has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:15.540
been arrested for casting 23 fraudulent votes for&nbsp;
her husband. Remember, voter fraud of this kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:25.140
is very rare. But when we find it, it's almost&nbsp;
always Republicans. Insider reports that Kim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:31.860
Fong Taylor was arrested and accused of multiple&nbsp;
counts of voter fraud. Prosecutors say that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:39.840
cast 23 fraudulent votes for her husband in the.&nbsp;
2020 election. Her husband, Jeremy Taylor, is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:46.620
elected Republican. There's an 11 page indictment.&nbsp;
It is wild. It claims that Kim Phuong Taylor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:52.140
quote, visited numerous households within the&nbsp;
Vietnamese community in Woodbury County. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.200
collected absentee ballots from people who weren't&nbsp;
there, filled them out, cast the ballots herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:04.140
quote, causing the casting of votes in the&nbsp;
names of residents who had no knowledge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.360
and had not consented to the casting of their&nbsp;
ballots. Taylor is also accused of signing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.920
voter registration forms on behalf of residents&nbsp;
who were not present. That's a crime. In total,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.200
it is 26 counts of providing false information,&nbsp;
three counts of fraudulent registration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:26.400
and 23 counts of fraudulent voting. Each charge&nbsp;
carries a maximum five year prison sentence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.840
Wow. The goal was to get her husband elected. I&nbsp;
want to remind people again and again and again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.560
and I will continue saying this until I don't need&nbsp;
to say it anymore. Voter fraud is very rare. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.520
also a pretty futile strategy that is not likely&nbsp;
to win an election. And the potential consequences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.400
of getting caught make it very much not worth&nbsp;
the risk. Up to five years potentially for each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.380
of those counts. She's not going to get, you know,&nbsp;
it's 50 counts total five years. She's not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:05.460
to get 250 years. I will bet any amount of money&nbsp;
on that. But the risk reward is very much out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.220
balance. Voter fraud is a really ineffective and&nbsp;
inefficient way to try to win an election because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:18.780
the number of fraudulent votes is almost always&nbsp;
too small to actually impact the outcome. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.380
risk of getting caught for voter fraud is high.&nbsp;
Now, Republicans will say everybody's getting away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.840
with voter fraud. All these Democrats are getting&nbsp;
away with it. The truth is, there is no reason to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.400
believe that that's the case. And we've seen the&nbsp;
Brennan Center for Justice study. The numbers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:39.300
the penalties for being caught are severe. It is&nbsp;
a really bad political strategy. It's relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:47.460
easily detected. And it would be better for these&nbsp;
people to spend their energy on activating voters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:52.680
help make the case that voters should vote for a&nbsp;
candidate because they think that that candidate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.320
would actually do good things for them. I&nbsp;
know it's like a crazy thing to think about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.300
but that would be a much better way to spend&nbsp;
your time. And the last element of this is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:07.500
When people get caught. It's almost always&nbsp;
Republicans, even though Republicans claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:12.540
it's Democrats that do this. Now, one&nbsp;
could say, David, Democrats are doing it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.100
but they're getting away with it. Republicans are&nbsp;
getting caught, but way more Democrats do it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.300
get away with it. Well, you've got to defend&nbsp;
that with some data. Why is it that Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.680
are so much smarter and able to get away with&nbsp;
it? There is no evidence of that whatsoever.

